     "type": "image",
     "src": "/images/6a8f58f0060d7a0b112b67b1_2236830423-p-2000.avif",
     "alt": ""
    }
   ],
   "html": "<p>The Masonic Lodge was transformed into a post-apocalyptic wasteland for an exclusive screening of the first four episodes of Marvel Zombies before its official debut on Disney+. </p>\n<p>Filmmakers, press, influencers, and Disney executives stepped into a fully immersive experience featuring gothic DJ Johnny HEALTH, fully zombified staff, and in-world decor. The night included undead-inspired F&amp;B, exclusive giveaways, photo moments, and a themed soda fountain all curated to drop attendees directly into the twisted universe.</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "DECOR",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "html": "<p><strong> </strong>In the courtyard, strewn debris, moody lighting, and heavy fog set the scene for the eerie evening. The fountain was transformed into a glowing Jones Soda display filled with dry ice and surrounded by lounge seating, high-tops, and branded bars for guests to enjoy. Upstairs, guests stepped into the Zombie Queen’s lair and the Hall of New Asgard’s Feast, complete with Blade’s iconic sword wall and faux fire goblets.</p>"
    },
